    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d983-a2">

                <pb facs="1120" n="1024" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1024"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>After a day and night of excitement, all business suspended, and rioting,
                    everything quiet at this hour. City heavily guarded. Soldiers <pb facs="1121"
                        n="1025" xml:id="pg1025"/> protect public squares and threatened points.
                    Mobs shouted yesterday “Death to Blanco and death to autonomy,” while “Viva
                    Weyler” was frequently heard. Contest between Spanish factions. Attention has
                    not yet been directed to other issues. Heard once yesterday of a few rioters
                    shouting a proposal to march to our consulate. Presence of ships may be
                    necessary later, but not now.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
